  "body": "Part of #31, the app and UI on wasm. This slice adds an **async file picker**, so a model or a project can be opened in the browser build. Until now every picker there answered \"cancelled\".\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0. The branch merges `upstream/main` (53a52f88) so that it diffs clean against `main`.\n\n## What changed\n- **`crates/ui/src/file_pick.rs`** (new): the browser picker. On wasm32, `open()` makes an `<input type=file>` whose `accept` comes from the dialog's filters, clicks it and returns at once. When the user has chosen, the file's name and bytes go into a thread-local inbox, and the next frame is woken through the egui context, which `shell_web` registers.\n  - Files over 256 MiB (`BROWSER_READ_LIMIT`) are refused by name before they are read. A failed allocation in wasm aborts the tab.\n  - The input and its change closure are held in one slot until the next pick, not `forget`ed, so a cancelled picker does not leak.\n  - The inbox, `accept_attr` and `too_big` are plain Rust on every target.\n- **`crates/ui/src/state_picked.rs`** (new):\n  - `open_model_dialog` / `open_project_dialog`: rfd's synchronous dialog on native (unchanged), the async picker on wasm32.\n  - Each frame, `drain_actions` turns every inbox entry into a `CommandKind::OpenPicked`. A model goes through `ImportModel::from_bytes` and `finish_import`: one undo step, and a same-named model is an update. A project goes through `project::open_noted`.\n  - A failed read, a refused import, or a project that is not text or not JSON is said on the status line (\"import refused: …\" / \"open failed: …\") and changes nothing.\n- **`crates/app/src/commands/import_model.rs`**: `ImportModel::from_bytes(file_name, data, budget)`. It shares the path import's laws through `checked_budget`: IGES and unknown extensions refused, the STEP budget's bounds. It adds the `MAX_FILE_BYTES` cap and the finite-mesh gate. `geometry::import::parse_model_graded_within` is now `pub`.\n- **`crates/ui/src/state.rs`**:\n  - Two new `CommandKind` arms route to the functions above.\n  - The model and project dialogs' filters are factored out (`mesh_dialog`, `project_dialog`) so both pickers ask with the same ones.\n  - `open_project_path`'s reset is factored out as `reset_for_open`, so the bytes open retires the old document the same way. Behaviour is unchanged.\n- No dependency added. The picker uses `eframe::web_sys` features that eframe already enables (`HtmlInputElement`, `File`, `FileList`, `Blob`).\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/31-wasm-file-picker.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- Pinning tests:\n  - `crates/app/tests/import_bytes.rs`:\n    - `picked_bytes_import_like_the_same_file_from_disk`: the same name, mesh and fidelity as the disk import, for STL, OBJ and STEP.\n    - `picked_bytes_are_refused_by_name_never_a_panic`: IGES, an unknown extension, no extension, empty or corrupt files of each format, and a budget given for a non-STEP file.\n  - `crates/ui/src/file_pick_tests.rs`:\n    - `a_picked_model_imports_through_the_undoable_command`\n    - `a_picked_file_that_cannot_be_used_is_refused_by_name`\n    - `a_picked_project_opens_in_place_of_the_document`\n    - `the_browser_picker_accepts_the_dialogs_extensions`\n    - `a_file_over_the_browser_read_limit_is_refused_before_it_is_read`\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green. The app suites (lib, import_bytes, large_models, model_fidelity, step_*, stock_export, bore_facet_sagitta) passed in 21 s. The ui suites (lib, boundary, boundary_picks, feedback, fixtures, gpu_render, machine, models, operations, shell, theme_files) passed in 19 s.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean (native, macOS).\n- **wasm check**: `web/build-app-wasm.sh` passed on macOS, using the official rustc 1.99.1 with the wasm32 std and Homebrew LLVM's clang for the wasi C.\n  - It linked `camcraft-cli.wasm` and `camcraft_ui.wasm`, ran wasm-bindgen 0.2.129 and laid out `target/web`. The shim answers all nine WASI imports.\n  - camcraft-ui raised no warnings.\n  - `web/check-app-page.sh target/web` passed.\n  - The script needed two local workarounds, which are not part of this PR: a GNU-`sed -i` shim, and a bash-3.2 empty-array fix for `\"${PROFILE_ARGS[@]}\"` under `set -u` (line 104). As shipped, the script does not run on stock macOS bash/sed. Worth a small follow-up.\n\n## Not exercised - browser hand check needed\n- **The picker was not run in a browser.** It needs a hand check: serve `target/web`, then use File > Open model on an STL, OBJ and STEP file and File > Open project on a `.camproj`. Also check that cancel does nothing and that a file over 256 MiB is refused on the status line.\n- The input is clicked from the egui frame (requestAnimationFrame), not from the DOM click handler itself. Browsers allow this within the click's transient user activation. That is the main thing to confirm by hand, Safari included.\n- Still owed on #31 (see the decisions file):\n  - Save, Save As and Post in the browser, which need a download.\n  - The other pickers: fixture import, machine, post, theme and tool library.\n  - Dropped files.\n  - Inline playback, a WebGPU run, the in-browser CI job, console diagnostics for the app crate, and the shell.rs split.\n\nChangelog: The browser build opens models (STL, OBJ, STEP) and projects through an async file picker (#31).\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #31\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
